// 26 U.S.C. §736, §737, §743(d), §751(b)-(f), §752(d), §753 — stage 2b:
// classification of payments to a retiring or deceased partner, gain
// recognized on a distribution of precontribution-gain property within 7
// years, the substantial-built-in-loss $250,000 test, the hot-asset/cold-
// asset exchange fiction on a distribution (unrealized receivables and
// substantially-appreciated inventory items), liabilities on a sale of a
// partnership interest, and income in respect of a decedent.
//
// JUDGMENT CALLS AND GAPS (see report):
//  - §736(a)/(b): the classification (distributive share / guaranteed
//    payment / section 751(b) sale-or-exchange distribution) is EXECUTABLE,
//    exported as `retiring_partner_payment_class`. §736(b)(2)'s exclusion of
//    unrealized-receivables and (non-agreement) goodwill payments from
//    "payments for an interest in partnership property" is EXECUTABLE, and
//    §736(b)(3)'s limitation (capital not a material income-producing
//    factor, general partner) gates it as an `unless` defeater, per the
//    statute's own "shall apply only if" phrasing.
//  - §737(a)-(d): the lesser-of formula is EXECUTABLE with intermediate
//    values (both operands of the "lesser of" exposed as their own
//    relations); the section 704(c)(1)(B) 7-year "net precontribution gain"
//    figure reuses module 08's own `section_704c1B_deemed_gain_or_loss`
//    machinery conceptually (net precontribution gain is a case-supplied
//    AGGREGATE over all such property per the finite-roster convention,
//    since summing every contributed property's own 704(c)(1)(B)-style
//    hypothetical gain needs a per-property enumeration this package's
//    `sum all … where` idiom can express once module 08's relation is keyed
//    per property — done here via `sum all`). §737(d)(1)'s second sentence
//    (interest-in-an-entity look-through) is TECH_GAP (TECH-GAPS.md G366;
//    needs the same entity-look-through machinery as section 731(c)(3)(A)(i)
//    / TECH-GAPS.md G362, not built).
//    §737(d)(2) and §737(e) are pure cross-references (to section 751(b),
//    already wired via a shared defeater name, and section 731(c), already
//    modeled in module 10) — NON_NORMATIVE, no new rule.
//  - §743(d): both the aggregate-excess test ((d)(1)(A)) and the
//    transferee-allocated-loss test ((d)(1)(B)) are EXECUTABLE, each on its
//    own $250,000 threshold, combined by an OR (two rules, same head, the
//    corpus's standard disjunction idiom) into a NEW relation
//    `section_743d_substantial_built_in_loss` — kept separate from module
//    06's existing CASE-ASSERTED `substantial_built_in_loss_after_transfer`
//    (an `empirical` relation; this compiler does not let a rule produce
//    into an `empirical`-kind relation, so the two coexist: a case that
//    wants the computed figure to drive section 743(b) asserts this
//    package's own institutional result into the empirical gate itself).
//    §743(d)(2)'s delegated regulations are EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY.
//  - §751(b): the exchange fiction is modeled directly from the statute's
//    own two exchange directions ((A) hot-for-other, (B) other-for-hot),
//    each a case-asserted "this much value crossed in this direction" fact
//    (Treas. Reg. 1.751-1(b)'s own proportionality computation over
//    pre-/post-distribution shares is NOT re-derived — EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY
//    for the exact proportionate SPLIT, EXECUTABLE for the exchange
//    classification and its two (b)(2) exceptions). Exported as
//    `section_751b_exchange`. (b)(3)(A)'s 120%-of-basis "substantially
//    appreciated" test is EXECUTABLE and exact; (b)(3)(B)'s anti-abuse
//    exclusion is a case-asserted defeater (a "principal purpose" test is
//    itself evaluative and not separately modeled beyond the flag).
//  - §751(c): the (1)-(2) core (rights to payment for goods/services not yet
//    includible) is EXECUTABLE; the second and third sentences (the long
//    list of section 1245/1250/1252/1253/1254/992/1248/617/1278/1283
//    recapture-type inclusions) are EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY/out of package scope
//    — none of those sections are imported by this package this stage;
//    modeled as an open case-asserted residual class, never invented.
//  - §751(d): (1)-(2) (section 1221(a)(1) property; other property that
//    would be non-capital-and-non-1231 on sale) are case-asserted
//    classifications (this package does not import section 1221/1231's own
//    machinery from `us.irc.property_transactions` for a PARTNERSHIP-level
//    inventory test, only for a PERSON's capital-asset test elsewhere); (3)
//    (the hypothetical "if held by the partner" test) is EXECUTABLE as its
//    own case-asserted classification, per the statute's own hypothetical
//    framing (this package does not re-run person-level tests hypothetically
//    against a different holder).
//  - §751(e) (the section 1248(b) tax-attributable limitation on a deemed
//    sale of section 1248 stock) is EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY (section 1248 is not
//    imported by this package). §751(f) (tiered-partnership look-through for
//    the unrealized-receivable/inventory tests) is TECH_GAP, the same
//    partnership-as-partner-of-a-partnership gap as section 706(d)(3)
//    (TECH-GAPS.md G361 already covers it; not filed twice).
//  - §752(d): EXECUTABLE — liabilities are added to the amount realized on
//    a sale of a partnership interest, the same as on a sale of property
//    generally (reusing the SHAPE of `us.irc.property_transactions::
//    amount_realized`'s own liability-inclusion principle, not a literal
//    cross-package derivation since that relation is typed to a general
//    `Transaction`/`Person` sale, not a partnership-interest-specific one).
//  - §753 (income in respect of a decedent under section 691) is a pure
//    cross-reference to a section this package does not implement
//    (`us.irc.estate_gift` or `us.irc.income_individual` territory) —
//    EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY, not reproduced.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irc.partnerships version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irc:partnerships:clir";

use self::{
    Asset,
    IRC_S736_A,
    IRC_S736_B,
    IRC_S737_A,
    IRC_S737_B,
    IRC_S743_D,
    IRC_S751_B,
    IRC_S751_C,
    IRC_S751_D,
    IRC_S752_D,
    Partnership,
    Person,
    Transaction,
    is_partner,
};

// ============================================================================
// §736: payments to a retiring or deceased partner
// ============================================================================

pub enum RetiringPartnerPaymentClass {
    DistributiveShare;
    GuaranteedPayment;
    Section751bExchangeDistribution;
    ExchangeForPartnershipProperty;
    label en unofficial "the four classifications section 736 sorts a liquidation payment into: (a)(1) distributive share, (a)(2) guaranteed payment, (b)(1) sale/exchange distribution for partnership property (net of the (b)(2) carve-outs), or (unlabeled residual) treated as a distribution for OTHER partnership property";
}

pub relation liquidation_payment_to_retiring_or_deceased_partner(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "a payment made in liquidation of the interest of a retiring partner or deceased partner (section 736 chapeau input)";
}
pub relation payment_determined_in_exchange_for_partnership_property(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the payment (or a portion of it) is determined, under regulations, to be made in exchange for the partner's interest in partnership property (section 736(b)(1) input) — the regulatory determination itself is not reproduced, this is the case's ultimate classification of the payment's character";
}
pub relation payment_for_unrealized_receivables_736(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the portion of the payment that is for unrealized receivables of the partnership (section 751(c)) (section 736(b)(2)(A) input)";
}
pub relation payment_for_goodwill_not_in_agreement(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the portion of the payment that is for partnership goodwill NOT provided for by the partnership agreement (section 736(b)(2)(B) input — a payment FOR goodwill that the agreement DOES provide for is not excluded)";
}
pub relation section_736b3_limitation_met(pship: Partnership, partner: Person) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "capital is not a material income-producing factor for the partnership, and the retiring or deceased partner was a general partner (section 736(b)(3)(A)-(B), the condition gating the (b)(2) exclusions)";
}

pub relation section_736b1_exchange_amount(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the portion of a liquidation payment treated as a distribution (section 731/732/751(b)) rather than a distributive share or guaranteed payment, because it is for the partner's interest in partnership property (section 736(b)(1)), after excluding unrealized-receivables and non-agreement-goodwill payments where section 736(b)(3) limits the property definition";
}
@source(IRC_S736_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Payments made in liquidation of the interest of a retiring partner or a deceased partner shall, to the extent such payments (other than payments described in paragraph (2)) are determined, under regulations prescribed by the Secretary, to be made in exchange for the interest of such partner in partnership property, be considered as a distribution by the partnership and not as a distributive share or guaranteed payment under subsection (a).")
rule S736b1ExchangeAmount(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) defeasible {
    label en official "a payment determined to be in exchange for the partner's interest in partnership property is treated as a distribution, not a distributive share or guaranteed payment (section 736(b)(1))";
    when payment_determined_in_exchange_for_partnership_property(t, pship, partner, amount);
    unless payment_for_unrealized_receivables_736(t, pship, partner, amount) and section_736b3_limitation_met(pship, partner) and payment_determined_in_exchange_for_partnership_property(t, pship, partner, amount);
    unless payment_for_goodwill_not_in_agreement(t, pship, partner, amount) and section_736b3_limitation_met(pship, partner) and payment_determined_in_exchange_for_partnership_property(t, pship, partner, amount);
    then section_736b1_exchange_amount(t, pship, partner, amount);
}

pub relation payment_determined_with_regard_to_income(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the amount of the payment is determined WITH regard to the income of the partnership (section 736(a) chapeau distinguishing (a)(1) from (a)(2))";
}
pub relation retiring_partner_payment_class(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money, class: RetiringPartnerPaymentClass) kind institutional {
    label en official "the section 736 classification of a liquidation payment to a retiring or deceased partner: a distributive share, a guaranteed payment, or (to the extent section 736(b)(1) applies) a distribution for partnership property (section 736(a)-(b))";
}
@source(IRC_S736_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "as a distributive share to the recipient of partnership income if the amount thereof is determined with regard to the income of the partnership, or")
rule S736a1DistributiveShare(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) defeasible {
    label en official "a liquidation payment determined with regard to partnership income is considered a distributive share (section 736(a)(1))";
    when liquidation_payment_to_retiring_or_deceased_partner(t, pship, partner, amount);
    when payment_determined_with_regard_to_income(t, pship, partner);
    unless section_736b1_exchange_amount(t, pship, partner, amount) and liquidation_payment_to_retiring_or_deceased_partner(t, pship, partner, amount);
    then retiring_partner_payment_class(t, pship, partner, amount, DistributiveShare);
}
@source(IRC_S736_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "as a guaranteed payment described in section 707(c) if the amount thereof is determined without regard to the income of the partnership")
rule S736a2GuaranteedPayment(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) defeasible {
    label en official "a liquidation payment determined without regard to partnership income is considered a section 707(c) guaranteed payment (section 736(a)(2))";
    when liquidation_payment_to_retiring_or_deceased_partner(t, pship, partner, amount);
    unless payment_determined_with_regard_to_income(t, pship, partner) and liquidation_payment_to_retiring_or_deceased_partner(t, pship, partner, amount);
    unless section_736b1_exchange_amount(t, pship, partner, amount) and liquidation_payment_to_retiring_or_deceased_partner(t, pship, partner, amount);
    then retiring_partner_payment_class(t, pship, partner, amount, GuaranteedPayment);
}
rule S736b1ClassIsExchange(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) defeasible {
    when section_736b1_exchange_amount(t, pship, partner, amount);
    then retiring_partner_payment_class(t, pship, partner, amount, ExchangeForPartnershipProperty);
}

// ============================================================================
// §737: precontribution gain on a distribution to a contributing partner
// ============================================================================

pub relation distribution_property_fmv_received(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the fair market value of property (other than money) received by the partner in the distribution (section 737(a)(1)(A) input)";
}
pub relation partner_outside_basis_before_737(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the partner's adjusted basis in the partnership interest immediately before the section 737 distribution (section 737(a)(1)(B) input)";
}
pub relation money_received_in_737_distribution(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the amount of money received in the section 737 distribution (section 737(a)(1)(B) reduction input)";
}
pub relation section_737a1_excess(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the section 737(a)(1) excess: FMV of property received over the partner's outside basis reduced (not below zero) by money received — the first operand of the section 737(a) lesser-of formula";
}
@source(IRC_S737_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the excess (if any) of (A) the fair market value of property (other than money) received in the distribution over (B) the adjusted basis of such partner's interest in the partnership immediately before the distribution reduced (but not below zero) by the amount of money received in the distribution, or")
rule S737a1Excess(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, fmv: Money, basis: Money, money: Money) strict {
    when distribution_property_fmv_received(t, pship, partner, fmv);
    when partner_outside_basis_before_737(t, pship, partner, basis);
    when money_received_in_737_distribution(t, pship, partner, money);
    then section_737a1_excess(t, pship, partner, max(0 USD, fmv - max(0 USD, basis - money)));
}

pub relation partner_contributed_property_704c1B_gain_component(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, prop: Asset, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the gain (if any) that would be recognized under section 704(c)(1)(B) with respect to one item of property the distributee partner contributed within 7 years, held by the partnership immediately before this distribution, as if it had been distributed to another partner (section 737(b) per-property input — this is the same 704(c)(1)(B) hypothetical module 08 computes for an ACTUAL distribution, supplied here for a HYPOTHETICAL one, per the statute's own cross-reference)";
}
pub relation section_737b_net_precontribution_gain(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the partner's net precontribution gain: the aggregate section 704(c)(1)(B) hypothetical gain over all property the partner contributed within 7 years and which the partnership still holds immediately before the distribution (section 737(b)) — the second operand of the section 737(a) lesser-of formula";
}
@source(IRC_S737_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "the term \"net precontribution gain\" means the net gain (if any) which would have been recognized by the distributee partner under section 704(c)(1)(B) if all property which")
rule S737bNetPrecontributionGain(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, some_prop: Asset) strict {
    when partner_contributed_property_704c1B_gain_component(t, pship, partner, some_prop, _);
    then section_737b_net_precontribution_gain(t, pship, partner,
        sum all a: Money for prop: Asset where partner_contributed_property_704c1B_gain_component(t, pship, partner, prop, a));
}

pub relation section_737_previously_contributed_property_exception(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "a portion of the property distributed consists of property which the distributee partner had previously contributed to the partnership (section 737(d)(1) exception input — the entity-interest look-through second sentence is TECH_GAP, see header note)";
}
relation section_737_751b_coordination_defeater(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "section 737 does not apply to the extent section 751(b) applies to the distribution (section 737(d)(2)) — case-asserted defeater flag shared with module 10's section 731(d) convention";
}

pub relation section_737_gain(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the gain the distributee partner is treated as recognizing under section 737(a): the lesser of the section 737(a)(1) excess or the section 737(b) net precontribution gain, in addition to any section 731 gain (section 737(a)-(b))";
}
@source(IRC_S737_A, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "such partner shall be treated as recognizing gain in an amount equal to the lesser of—")
rule S737Gain(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, excess: Money, net_gain: Money) defeasible {
    label en official "the section 737(a) gain is the lesser of the FMV-over-basis excess and the net precontribution gain (section 737(a))";
    when section_737a1_excess(t, pship, partner, excess);
    when section_737b_net_precontribution_gain(t, pship, partner, net_gain);
    unless section_737_previously_contributed_property_exception(t, pship, partner) and section_737a1_excess(t, pship, partner, excess) and section_737b_net_precontribution_gain(t, pship, partner, net_gain);
    unless section_737_751b_coordination_defeater(t, pship) and section_737a1_excess(t, pship, partner, excess) and section_737b_net_precontribution_gain(t, pship, partner, net_gain);
    then section_737_gain(t, pship, partner, min(excess, net_gain));
}

pub relation section_737c1_basis_increase(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the partner's outside basis is increased by the amount of gain recognized under section 737(a), treated as occurring immediately before the distribution for purposes of the section 732 basis of distributed property (section 737(c)(1))";
}
rule S737c1BasisIncrease(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, gain: Money) defeasible {
    when section_737_gain(t, pship, partner, gain);
    then section_737c1_basis_increase(t, pship, partner, gain);
}
pub relation section_737c2_partnership_basis_adjustment(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, prop: Asset, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the appropriate adjustment made to the partnership's basis in the contributed property referred to in section 737(b), to reflect the section 737(a) gain (section 737(c)(2)) — a case-computed figure, this package does not derive the 'appropriate' allocation among possibly several contributed properties generically";
}

// ============================================================================
// §743(d): substantial built-in loss
// ============================================================================

pub relation partnership_aggregate_basis_in_property(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the partnership's aggregate adjusted basis in partnership property, at the time of the transfer (section 743(d)(1)(A) input)";
}
pub relation partnership_aggregate_fmv_of_property(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the aggregate fair market value of partnership property, at the time of the transfer (section 743(d)(1)(A) input)";
}
pub relation transferee_hypothetical_loss_if_sold(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, transferee: Person, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the loss the transferee partner would be allocated if the partnership assets were sold for cash equal to their fair market value immediately after the transfer (section 743(d)(1)(B) input)";
}

pub relation section_743d_substantial_built_in_loss(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership) kind institutional {
    label en official "the partnership has a substantial built-in loss with respect to the transfer: either the aggregate basis exceeds aggregate FMV by more than $250,000, or the transferee would be allocated a loss of more than $250,000 on a hypothetical cash sale (section 743(d)(1)(A)-(B))";
}
@source(IRC_S743_D, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the partnership's adjusted basis in the partnership property exceeds by more than $250,000 the fair market value of such property, or")
rule S743d1AAggregateExcess(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, basis: Money, fmv: Money) strict {
    when partnership_aggregate_basis_in_property(t, pship, basis);
    when partnership_aggregate_fmv_of_property(t, pship, fmv);
    when (basis - fmv) > 250000.00 USD;
    then section_743d_substantial_built_in_loss(t, pship);
}
@source(IRC_S743_D, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "the transferee partner would be allocated a loss of more than $250,000 if the partnership assets were sold for cash equal to their fair market value immediately after such transfer")
rule S743d1BTransfereeLoss(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, transferee: Person, loss: Money) strict {
    when transferee_hypothetical_loss_if_sold(t, pship, transferee, loss);
    when loss > 250000.00 USD;
    then section_743d_substantial_built_in_loss(t, pship);
}
relation section_743d2_regulations(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY (section 743(d)(2): delegated regulations aggregating related partnerships and disregarding anti-avoidance property acquisitions) — cross-reference, not reproduced";
}

// ============================================================================
// §751(b): distributions treated as sales or exchanges (hot/cold assets)
// ============================================================================

pub relation partner_receives_hot_assets_for_other_interest(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, hot_prop: Asset, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the partner receives, in the distribution, unrealized receivables or substantially-appreciated inventory items, in exchange for all or part of the partner's interest in OTHER partnership property (including money) (section 751(b)(1)(A) input — the exact proportionate value crossing hands is a case-computed figure, Treas. Reg. 1.751-1(b)'s own formula is not re-derived, see header note)";
}
pub relation partner_receives_other_property_for_hot_interest(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, other_prop: Asset, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the partner receives, in the distribution, partnership property (including money) OTHER than unrealized receivables/substantially-appreciated inventory, in exchange for all or part of the partner's interest in such hot assets (section 751(b)(1)(B) input)";
}
pub relation section_751b_distributee_contributed_property_exception(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, prop: Asset) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the property distributed is property the distributee contributed to the partnership (section 751(b)(2)(A) exception input)";
}

pub relation section_751b_exchange(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, prop: Asset, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the distribution is considered a sale or exchange of property between the distributee and the partnership (as constituted after the distribution), under section 751(b)(1), for the hot-for-other or other-for-hot value crossing hands, unless a section 751(b)(2) exception applies";
}
@source(IRC_S751_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "such transactions shall, under regulations prescribed by the Secretary, be considered as a sale or exchange of such property between the distributee and the partnership (as constituted after the distribution)")
rule S751bExchangeHotForOther(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, hot_prop: Asset, amount: Money) defeasible {
    label en official "a partner who receives hot assets in exchange for an interest in other partnership property is treated as selling/exchanging that property with the partnership (section 751(b)(1)(A))";
    when partner_receives_hot_assets_for_other_interest(t, pship, partner, hot_prop, amount);
    unless section_751b_distributee_contributed_property_exception(t, pship, partner, hot_prop) and partner_receives_hot_assets_for_other_interest(t, pship, partner, hot_prop, amount);
    unless liquidation_payment_to_retiring_or_deceased_partner(t, pship, partner, amount) and payment_determined_with_regard_to_income(t, pship, partner) and partner_receives_hot_assets_for_other_interest(t, pship, partner, hot_prop, amount);
    then section_751b_exchange(t, pship, partner, hot_prop, amount);
}
rule S751bExchangeOtherForHot(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, partner: Person, other_prop: Asset, amount: Money) defeasible {
    label en official "a partner who receives other partnership property in exchange for an interest in hot assets is treated as selling/exchanging that property with the partnership (section 751(b)(1)(B))";
    when partner_receives_other_property_for_hot_interest(t, pship, partner, other_prop, amount);
    unless section_751b_distributee_contributed_property_exception(t, pship, partner, other_prop) and partner_receives_other_property_for_hot_interest(t, pship, partner, other_prop, amount);
    then section_751b_exchange(t, pship, partner, other_prop, amount);
}

pub relation inventory_item_fmv(pship: Partnership, item: Asset, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the fair market value of an inventory item held by the partnership (section 751(b)(3)(A) input)";
}
pub relation inventory_item_partnership_basis(pship: Partnership, item: Asset, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the adjusted basis of the inventory item to the partnership (section 751(b)(3)(A) input)";
}
pub relation inventory_acquired_to_avoid_751(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "a principal purpose for acquiring this inventory property was to avoid section 751(b)'s inventory-item provisions (section 751(b)(3)(B) exclusion input)";
}
pub relation section_751b3_substantially_appreciated(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind institutional {
    label en official "the inventory item has appreciated substantially in value: its fair market value exceeds 120 percent of its adjusted basis to the partnership (section 751(b)(3)(A)), unless excluded as acquired to avoid this subsection (section 751(b)(3)(B))";
}
@source(IRC_S751_B, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "Inventory items of the partnership shall be considered to have appreciated substantially in value if their fair market value exceeds 120 percent of the adjusted basis to the partnership of such property.")
rule S751b3SubstantiallyAppreciated(pship: Partnership, item: Asset, fmv: Money, basis: Money) defeasible {
    when inventory_item_fmv(pship, item, fmv);
    when inventory_item_partnership_basis(pship, item, basis);
    when fmv > round(1.20 * basis, 2, "HALF_UP");
    unless inventory_acquired_to_avoid_751(pship, item) and inventory_item_fmv(pship, item, fmv) and inventory_item_partnership_basis(pship, item, basis);
    then section_751b3_substantially_appreciated(pship, item);
}

// ============================================================================
// §751(c)-(d): unrealized receivables and inventory items (definitions)
// ============================================================================

pub relation right_to_payment_for_goods_ordinary_character(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "a right (contractual or otherwise) to payment for goods delivered or to be delivered, not previously includible in income, the proceeds of which would be ordinary income (not from a capital asset) (section 751(c)(1) input)";
}
pub relation right_to_payment_for_services(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "a right (contractual or otherwise) to payment for services rendered or to be rendered, not previously includible in income (section 751(c)(2) input)";
}
pub relation is_unrealized_receivable_751c(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind institutional {
    label en official "the right is an 'unrealized receivable' within section 751(c): a right to payment for goods (ordinary character) or services, not previously includible in income (section 751(c)(1)-(2)) — the further recapture-type inclusions of section 751(c)'s second and third sentences (sections 1245/1250/1252/1253/1254/992/1248/617/1278/1283) are EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY, not reproduced";
}
@source(IRC_S751_C, relation = formalizes, coverage = partial, quote = "the term \"unrealized receivables\" includes, to the extent not previously includible in income under the method of accounting used by the partnership, any rights (contractual or otherwise) to payment for—")
rule S751cGoodsReceivable(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) strict {
    when right_to_payment_for_goods_ordinary_character(pship, item);
    then is_unrealized_receivable_751c(pship, item);
}
rule S751cServicesReceivable(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) strict {
    when right_to_payment_for_services(pship, item);
    then is_unrealized_receivable_751c(pship, item);
}
relation section_751c_recapture_residual(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY (section 751(c) second/third sentences: mining property, DISC stock, section 1245/1248/1250/1252/1253/1254 property, market discount bonds, short-term obligations — none of the underlying sections are imported by this package) — case-asserted only";
}

pub relation is_1221a1_property(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the property is of the kind described in section 1221(a)(1) (stock in trade, inventory, or property held for sale to customers) (section 751(d)(1) input — a case-asserted classification, this package's own section 1221 test lives at the PERSON level in us.irc.property_transactions, not the partnership-inventory level section 751(d) needs)";
}
pub relation would_be_ordinary_on_sale_by_partnership(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "on sale or exchange by the partnership, the property would be considered property other than a capital asset and other than section 1231 property (section 751(d)(2) input)";
}
pub relation would_be_1221a1_or_ordinary_in_partner_hands(partner: Person, item: Asset) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "if held by the selling or distributee partner, the property would be considered property of the type described in section 751(d)(1) or (2) (section 751(d)(3) hypothetical input)";
}

pub relation is_inventory_item_751d(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) kind institutional {
    label en official "the property is an 'inventory item' within section 751(d): section 1221(a)(1) property, other property that would be non-capital/non-1231 on the partnership's own sale, or property that would be such in the selling or distributee partner's hands (section 751(d)(1)-(3))";
}
@source(IRC_S751_D, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "property of the partnership of the kind described in section 1221(a)(1),")
rule S751d1Section1221a1(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) strict {
    when is_1221a1_property(pship, item);
    then is_inventory_item_751d(pship, item);
}
@source(IRC_S751_D, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "any other property of the partnership which, on sale or exchange by the partnership, would be considered property other than a capital asset and other than property described in section 1231,")
rule S751d2OrdinaryOnSale(pship: Partnership, item: Asset) strict {
    when would_be_ordinary_on_sale_by_partnership(pship, item);
    then is_inventory_item_751d(pship, item);
}
@source(IRC_S751_D, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "any other property held by the partnership which, if held by the selling or distributee partner, would be considered property of the type described in paragraph (1) or (2)")
rule S751d3HypotheticalInPartnerHands(pship: Partnership, partner: Person, item: Asset) strict {
    when is_partner(partner, pship);
    when would_be_1221a1_or_ordinary_in_partner_hands(partner, item);
    then is_inventory_item_751d(pship, item);
}

// --- §751(e)-(f): cross-references and tiered-partnership look-through -----

relation section_751e_1248b_limitation(t: Transaction, pship: Partnership, individual: Person, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY (section 751(e): the section 1248(b) tax-attributable limitation on a deemed sale of section 1248 stock — section 1248 is not imported by this package) — case-asserted only";
}
relation section_751f_tiered_partnership_lookthrough(pship: Partnership, lower_tier: Partnership, item: Asset) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "TECH_GAP (TECH-GAPS.md G361): section 751(f)'s tiered-partnership look-through needs the same 'partnership is a partner of another partnership' fact section 706(d)(3) needs, which this package's is_partner(partner: Person, …) does not type — not modeled";
}

// ============================================================================
// §752(d): liabilities on a sale or exchange of a partnership interest
// ============================================================================

pub relation interest_sale_consideration_received(t: Transaction, seller: Person, pship: Partnership, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the consideration (other than liability relief) received by the seller on a sale or exchange of the partnership interest (section 752(d) input)";
}
pub relation seller_share_of_liabilities_relieved_on_sale(t: Transaction, seller: Person, pship: Partnership, amount: Money) kind empirical {
    label en unofficial "the seller's share of partnership liabilities from which the seller is relieved by reason of the sale (section 752(d) input)";
}
pub relation section_752d_amount_realized(t: Transaction, seller: Person, pship: Partnership, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en official "the amount realized on a sale or exchange of a partnership interest includes the seller's share of partnership liabilities, treated the same as liabilities in connection with a sale or exchange of property generally (section 752(d))";
}
@source(IRC_S752_D, relation = formalizes, coverage = exact, quote = "In the case of a sale or exchange of an interest in a partnership, liabilities shall be treated in the same manner as liabilities in connection with the sale or exchange of property not associated with partnerships.")
rule S752dAmountRealizedIncludesLiabilities(t: Transaction, seller: Person, pship: Partnership, consideration: Money, liabilities: Money) strict {
    when interest_sale_consideration_received(t, seller, pship, consideration);
    when seller_share_of_liabilities_relieved_on_sale(t, seller, pship, liabilities);
    then section_752d_amount_realized(t, seller, pship, consideration + liabilities);
}

// ============================================================================
// §753: income in respect of a decedent
// ============================================================================

relation section_753_income_in_respect_of_decedent(successor: Person, pship: Partnership, amount: Money) kind institutional {
    label en unofficial "EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY (section 753: an amount includible in a deceased partner's successor's gross income under section 736(a) is income in respect of a decedent under section 691 — section 691 is not imported by this package) — case-asserted only";
}
